PHYSICAL-GLASS SEQUENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ ] 1. Upgrade an existing RangeWater 1.2.0 installation containing a saved straight plan.
[ ] 2. Confirm all accepted ranch records, preferences, help behavior, and calculations survive.
[ ] 3. Confirm the former straight plan appears unchanged and accepts another divider.
[ ] 4. Create multiple dividers in one pasture and at least one in another pasture.
[ ] 5. Quarter a pasture or create another valid layout with at least three regions.
[ ] 6. Route a waypoint divider around a real or representative obstacle.
[ ] 7. Exercise endpoint and waypoint Add, Move, Remove, Undo, Cancel, and Save.
[ ] 8. Confirm region acreages reconcile to the parent and survive a cold reopen.
[ ] 9. Confirm one pasture's plan never removes or disables another pasture's plan.
[ ] 10. Create a shared interior junction, move it, and verify every referencing line and region.
[ ] 11. Attempt to delete the referenced junction and confirm the operation is blocked.
[ ] 12. Archive and delete one referencing divider; verify remaining geometry and references.
[ ] 13. Cross or drag onto a private waypoint and confirm no silent sharing occurs.
[ ] 14. Use Connect / Share and verify atomic promotion, connection, and plan validation.
[ ] 15. Confirm shared-junction demotion is blocked; unlink safely, then demote when valid.
[ ] 16. Create all seven Field Ledger record types at precise map points.
[ ] 17. Create a Task, complete it, reopen it, edit it, and archive it.
[ ] 18. Verify manual map placement with device location permission denied.
[ ] 19. Exercise foreground location and verify displayed accuracy and the saved point.
[ ] 20. Filter by type, pasture, status, and archive state; select a result on the map.
[ ] 21. Edit a pasture boundary and confirm historical Field Ledger coordinates do not move.
[ ] 22. Create a format-4 backup, restore it on the other device, and verify plans and records.
[ ] 23. Restore a known format-3 backup and verify the legacy plan migrates without redraw.
[ ] 24. Use Undo Last Restore and confirm the complete prior state returns.

